node_modules/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. .env.example is the tracked template and must never hold a real key.
.env
.env.local

# Runtime artefacts: uploads and extracted frames are regenerated on every run.
.tmp/
public/frames/

# Personal Claude Code overrides. .claude/settings.json is shared and stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Tool cache. .impeccable/config.json is a real project decision and stays tracked.
.impeccable/hook.cache.json

# General-purpose Claude Code skills that came with the machine, not with this
# project: 4.8 MB across 179 files of design tooling a reviewer has no reason to
# read. The four skills this project actually defines stay tracked below.
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/run-observation/
!.claude/skills/schema-mirror/
!.claude/skills/ground-truth-check/
!.claude/skills/phase-report/

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED, and why. These four paths are the submission's
# evidence, not build output:
#
#   fixtures/videos/*.mp4   the brief says "Provide the recordings" (~45 MB)
#   fixtures/timelines/     what the model observed, per recording
#   fixtures/guides/        the produced guides
#   fixtures/verdicts/      every grounding verdict, with its quoted evidence
#
# Committing them is what makes `npm run guide -- fixtures/videos/A.mp4` rebuild
# a complete guide from a clean clone with **no API key and no network**, which
# is the reproducibility claim in README.md and DELIVERY_NOTES.md. Ignoring them
# would leave a reviewer with a repository that cannot demonstrate its own
# result, and would make both documents untrue.
#
# If they ever do need to go, uncomment together and fix both documents:
#   fixtures/videos/*.mp4
#   fixtures/timelines/
#   fixtures/guides/
#   fixtures/verdicts/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
